      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T10:42:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not strictly true. It doesn\u0027t *always* generate them. What it does is *always* generate a ninja rule that can be used to generate them.\n\nIt seems to me that this will make `checkbuild` take longer as we\u0027re going to be generate src jars for every library, not just the handful on the bootclasspath.\n\nThere is logic to detect whether a module is on the bootclasspath so you could use that to make this better. However, I doubt that the build team would like yet more magic in Soong. AIUI Roboleaf/Bazel prefer being explicit to magic.\n\nWhy not just add `include_srcs\u003dtrue` to every library that is part of the bootclasspath? A lot more tedious but longer term probably the best way to handle it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "3a691bda2abfb508b8189c25d633d98d2db61aec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9df6ab37_f098fde9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T11:06:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s slightly more complicated as it\u0027s not just the srcs of the libraries that are included directly on the bootclasspath but also any libraries that are statically included in them.",
      "parentUuid": "c28daede_90c8a39b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "3a691bda2abfb508b8189c25d633d98d2db61aec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
